  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) As per molecular formula<br /><br /><math><mtext>C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math><br /><br />(ii) As we know in case of percentage, the total mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math><br /><br />(iii) When total mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math><br /><br />the mass of oxygen <math><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math><br /><br />So, when total mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math><br /><br />Percentage of oxygen <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>53.33</mn><mtext>%</mtext></math>",
